view: a program and its view, and the messages between them

A program says what to show as nodes; a view draws them and hands back
what the person did. fm does what a file manager does and ed what an
editor does; how either is shown is the view's: the terminal on tty
(`view/term.go`), gio's window (`gio/README`), a page next. Nodes, not
cells: cells would make the page a terminal in a browser, as ttyd does,
where nodes let a view draw a pill or a chip.

    type View interface {
        Draw(n *Node, status string, state []string)
        Key() (Key, bool)
        Ask(prompt, def string) (string, bool)
        Size() (w, h int)
        Copy(text string) error
    }

Messages, not calls
  A program and its view pass only plain data: in one process a call
  whose arguments are data, down a pipe or a socket a JSON line each
  (`outline/outline.go:/msg is one line on the wire/`).
    to the view      draw: the tree, the program's word and its state;
                     ask: a prompt; copy: text for the clipboard
    to the program   key: its name, the node it was said on, the rune a
                     click fell on, any text; answer: the line typed;
                     size: how much the view shows
  A message joins when a view needs one. What only a terminal can do
  stays with it, and a window says so.

Who holds what
  program  the data, the cursor and the selection: what its verbs act on.
           fm sends the folder it stands in, ed every line, its cursor
           and its selection as runs.
  view     how it shows: a folder as rows or as thumbs, t turning between
           them. It moves the cursor among what it shows, and tells the
           program where it landed; going in and out is the program's,
           for it changes what is shown.
  between  ideas, by name: down, in, rename. A key is one way to say one
           and a click another; ed passes its keys through, for an
           editor's keys are its language.

The status line, at the bottom only, in every view
  The program's word on the left, what just happened or what it asks; on
  the right its state, [2] selected, cut:3, mark:x, then the view's, its
  layout and where the cursor is. ed says its mode, + while unsaved,
  held while that keeps it from cur's file, and line:col. A prompt takes
  the line while it asks.

The structure is the tree, not a language
  Folders and files carry it down to the idea, and inside a file the
  note's own indent carries the rest. A primitive is a kind the views
  know, a package of its own as sys/picture is, asked by kind: no plugin
  system and no runtime library. fm and ed stay programs, each at the end
  of messages; as Go packages one process could host both, which stays
  open.
